# f0 = the module, f2 = read
# `{ __proto__: null, get, set }` is how the library writes every descriptor: nothing that somebody lays on Object.prototype can come into it. SetLiteralPrototype counted as a way out of sight, so the scan gave the descriptor up and Link knew no accessor: every read of the name went by name.
# A literal whose prototype is set to null in its own text still holds only what its body lays: null above it can add nothing, and the operation hands the object to nobody.
